  <section|Source-to-mathematics notes><label|source-to-mathematics-notes>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|Delay.monitor_pays> proves the monitor dominates every
    fixed power of the logarithmic bill. The manuscript also expands the
    asymptotic comparison: with fixed block side, <verbatim|betaF=x+O(1)>,
    <verbatim|radiusB\<leq\>1+(log x)^2>, and <verbatim|log H=(log log
    betaF)^2>, so every fixed polynomial in the radii is <verbatim|H^{o(1)}>.

    <item><verbatim|Quince.\<varepsilon\>Goal> is exactly the finite sum over
    derivative orders of ordered-finpartition counts, <verbatim|2^j>, the
    strip tail, the degree-growth constant to power <verbatim|j>, and the
    selected rights fee. The displayed proof explains why every summand has a
    strict negative rate, and why multiplication by the monitor factor still
    tends to zero.

    <item><verbatim|Grade.horizon_u> compares the actual response-plus-paint
    cost against <verbatim|uval>. The manuscript expands the three rust
    components: segment, tranche, and scratch. The powers in
    <verbatim|fuse=8+2p+2pn> dominate respectively <verbatim|2p+pn>,
    <verbatim|2p>, and <verbatim|8+2pn>. The source's coefficients are
    <verbatim|boost=blaze+(blaze+1)L^3+haze> and
    <verbatim|aprice=boost*bulk(packing)^fuse+16/D.epsilon>.

    <item><verbatim|Grade.scales_m> uses two separate consequences of
    <verbatim|chi*U*K\<rightarrow\>0>: first, <verbatim|F\<leq\>1> from
    <verbatim|chi\<geq\>1> and <verbatim|K\<geq\>1>; second, <verbatim|d_*
    chi U K\<leq\>y> with <verbatim|d_*=1+clocks(1)>, combined with linearity
    of <verbatim|clocks(t)>. The head moment is expanded from
    <verbatim|meter=2(1+heads)^{m+1}inflate_m> with <verbatim|m=4(n+1)>.

    <item>The support geometry has the exact formulas
    <verbatim|radiusB=ceil((log x)^2)>, <verbatim|radiusD=b(4b+2)+2b>,
    <verbatim|reach=45(1+b)>, <verbatim|depthW=L(R+2)>,
    <verbatim|breadth=q(4B.B+2)+2B.B+8>, and <verbatim|scope=r*b+breadth+1>.
    The manuscript proves the bulk comparison used in <verbatim|Lute.covers>
    from these displayed formulas; it does not replace reach by the unrelated
    local cover-radius parameter <verbatim|r>.

    <item>The scalar response cost <verbatim|F> is explicitly expanded as
    segment + tranche + scratch + the <verbatim|16/D.epsilon> response charge
    + the fine-level paint term. The paint loom is evaluated at
    <verbatim|radiusD>; the rust loom is evaluated at <verbatim|reach>.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Remaining inputs and verification><label|remaining-inputs-and-verification>

  This chapter does not produce <verbatim|Carrier.priced>, the selected strip
  estimate, <verbatim|Ramble.gathered> coefficient growth, the weighted
  killed-jet receipt, the healthy chart and same-history placement, or the
  upstream <verbatim|Li.decade>/Medal construction inputs. It proves the rate
  and scale implications actually used after those inputs are supplied.
  Source inspection used <verbatim|rg -n> and <verbatim|sed -n> on the listed
  files and immediate definitions. No Lean or TeX build was run.
  <verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was run; in this isolated
  clone it stops because parent-owned <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>
  is absent.

